{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 ~19:50 PST (workstream C2, second pass).\n- Bug reddish-drinkable-canvasback: CLOSED. Root cause was an OOM kill of the MCP container mid fast-forward (2026-10-28 17:47 PDT). Fix 3355 (d583578c4da) does 2 things: the entrypoint recovers a provably interrupted fast-forward, and the autodeploy tick pages via deploy_errors when the live workspace is dirty, unreadable, or behind its image commit. It is deployed. The MCP close path now verifies against current main with sonnet-5-5.\n- Bedrock alarm Terraform: the plan (via the wrapper) is limited to the 6 ModelId dimension changes on rebar-bedrock-invoke-client-errors. The apply was refused by the session's auto-mode permission classifier (\"Protected-Scope IaC Apply\"), so it is NOT applied. The operator, or a session whose permissions allow IaC apply, runs: `cd <worktree at origin/main> && AWS_PROFILE=frontier scripts/terraform_prod.py plan --out <scratch>/plan.tfplan && AWS_PROFILE=frontier scripts/terraform_prod.py apply <scratch>/plan.tfplan`. The 4 bedrock-cache-ratio-low-* / bedrock-unit-cost-high-* alarms are not in Terraform at all.\n- New bug filed, not worked: juiced-anarthrous-bird. The MCP workspace refreshes only at container start, so closes between MCP-path deploys verify against the last MCP deploy's commit.\n- skilled-cepevorous-naga: plan certified earlier; another session appears to own implementation (an engine-switch worktree exists). Not touched."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794454922519352761,"uuid":"a08b6b70-8e4e-45fe-86e5-9d857506cd2d"}